# `.squad/` is what this system produces. Two halves with opposite answers, and the
# arrangement is copied from the kit's own `.gitignore` rather than invented here.
#
#   wiki/     durable knowledge — decisions, references. It travels.
#   records/  the dated trail — one run's plans, briefs, audits, reviews. It does not:
#             what this machine's cycles did says nothing to whoever clones, and
#             committing it puts one operator's run history in everybody's diff.
#
# TWO exceptions, each argued rather than convenient:
#
#   domain-routing.txt   the map deciding which specialist owns which repository. It is
#                        CONFIGURATION, not a run record, and a clone without it routes
#                        by nothing (B-008).
#   records/acceptance/  the evidence that a milestone was exercised against a released
#                        artifact. It is what an auditor reads to answer "was this ever
#                        actually used before we called it done", and an answer only one
#                        machine can read is not an answer (B-020).
#
# `.squad/*` and not `.squad/`: git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so the
# star is what lets the re-inclusions below be reachable at all.
.squad/*
!.squad/domain-routing.txt
!.squad/wiki/
!.squad/records/
.squad/records/*
!.squad/records/acceptance/
